From 81a6ecbe9179b0d0c0738e2d80613f164d3e19ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdous Bhai <ferdousbd@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:21:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add splice_tree to edit a tree at given paths

Add `Repository::splice_tree(root, edits)` and the `TreeEdit` enum (Put,
PutFile, Delete). Only the trees on the paths from each edit to the root
are read and rewritten; all other subtrees keep their ids, so the cost of
a new snapshot follows the size of the change rather than the size of the
source. This suits continuous sync, where a watcher already knows which
paths changed.

Also add `Repository::save_snapshot`, which returns the id of the saved
snapshot so it can be used as the next snapshot's parent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
